# Build output and dependencies
node_modules/
dist/

# Playwright run artefacts. The BASELINES are not here - they live in
# tests/**/*-snapshots/ and are committed on purpose: a reference image that is
# not in version control is not a reference, and the visual gate would compare
# each run against whatever the last run happened to produce.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Full gate output, kept so a red can be classified after the run ends (a load
# timeout is UNMEASURED, a real assertion is FAIL - and the difference is only
# readable in the error text). Playwright wipes test-results/ between projects
# and the `list` reporter writes no file, so without this the evidence died
# with the stage.
gate-logs/

# TRAP, learned the hard way: do NOT add a secrets pattern such as
# `credentials*` or `secrets*` here "to be safe". On a case-insensitive
# filesystem (Windows, macOS default) it silently ignores a NEW source file
# named `Credentials*.tsx` or `SecretsPanel.tsx`: the file exists locally, the
# gates are green locally, and CI is red on a module that does not exist in
# the commit. The secret scan (scripts/secret-scan.sh) guards content; this
# file guards artefacts. If such a pattern must exist, anchor it to the root
# (`/credentials.json`) rather than a glob.
